y to apple  and it makes sense for apple to utilize  it because  it truly is groundbreaking but now let's  get into how i know apple is going to be  utilizing it  and why it's going to make apple  dominate the market for the next couple  of years  a couple of months back mark german who  is by far the most reliable apple leaker  reported that apple is getting new  high-end macs ready  including the macbook pros the mac mini  the larger imac  and the mac pro but within that report  he gave us some very interesting details  in terms of the chips that apple will be  using for the macbook pros  there will be two chips codenamed jade c  chop and jade c die both with eight high  performance cores  two efficiency cores and either 16 or 32  graphic scores  so the only difference between the two  is the graphics  but here's what i only just now realized  jdc dye stands for the full die  with 32 gpu cores and jtc  chop means that apple will literally be  chopping off  16 of the graphics cores from the  full-size  chip to make a weaker chip which will  probably be going into the base model  16-inch macbook pro  as well as the 14 inch model this will  essentially allow apple  to mass manufacture a single m1x chip  to save a ton of cash while at the same  time  creating the illusion of a variety of  chip options  which will give apple the chance to  upsell chip  upgrades with better performance so for  example  the base 14 inch macbook pro could get a  binned 12 core gpu version of the jade c  chop with apple disabling up to four  potentially defective gpu cores  which is something apple is already  doing with the base m1 macbook air's  7 core gpu to give them better chip  yields  now on top of the base 14 inch model  apple could allow  you to upgrade to the 16 core jc  chop chip for maybe 150 dollars more  or maybe even spend 300 more to upgrade  to a  bend 24 or 28 core version  of the full size jade c die chip  and then for the 16 inch macbook pro  you'll get the 16 core jtc 