0 core  mac pro cpu chip and then take the m1x's  32 core gpu and multiply it by four  to give you the full 128 cores  and that's why it makes so much sense  for the mac pro's highest end  jade four cdi chip to have eight  efficiency cores  since it's literally gonna combine four  of the regular m1x chips together  which each contain two efficiency cores  but here's the absolutely genius part  about  all of this apple will essentially be  mass producing  insane amounts of that same exact m1x  jdc die chip to cover a wide variety of  macs  like the lower end 14 inch macbook pro  all the way up to a high  end 40 core mac pro and they could even  throw in  the 20 core jade 2c die into other  products like a new apple silicon imac  pro  or a very high-end mac mini if they  wanted to  and they're all going to be using a  single m1x chip design  saving them unspeakable amounts of cash  this level of mass manufacturing is  going to allow apple to subsidize their  max  and keep the prices impressively low for  how much power these new chips pack  making it very difficult for other pc  makers like qualcomm  to compete since they won't be able to  mass manufacture chips  like apple will be able to do and that  is how apple is going to be dominating  the pc market for the next couple of  years  especially in the laptop market the only  question remaining  is whether these chips will be called  the m1x or the m2x  especially since the apple silicon mac  pro isn't expected to come  until late in 2022 but either way  apple's gonna be killing it with this  chiplet technology  if you totally disagree with my thoughts  on this then go ahead and comment your  thoughts down below  but if you enjoyed this video click that  circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one and definitely  check out one of those two right over  there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one

